        <item>
            <title>1.0.7</title>
            <pubDate>Tue, 08 Sep 2026 15:30:17 -0400</pubDate>
            <sparkle:version>1.0.7</sparkle:version>
            <sparkle:shortVersionString>1.0.7</sparkle:shortVersionString>
            <sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>14.0</sparkle:minimumSystemVersion>
            <description sparkle:format="markdown"><![CDATA[### Drawing on GIFs

Make a GIF from a recording and you can now write on it first. Scrub to a
moment, type or draw, and it stays on screen from there. Reached the same way
as before — ⌘G on a recording, or Make GIF in the trim window.

There is white in the palette now, and a seventh swatch that opens the colour
picker if you need to match something exactly.

### Moving around the panel

The arrows are spatial in the picture grid: left and right move to the
thumbnail beside this one, up and down to the one above or below. ⇥ switches
between text and pictures, and it returns you to where you were rather than to
the top. Opening the panel always starts at the top.

### Fixes

- The right-click menu on a thumbnail did nothing at all. Every item works now,
  and Edit and Share have been added to it.
- Pressing a digit without Accessibility permission quietly reordered your list
  instead of pasting. It now says what is wrong and offers to open the settings.
- Nothing opens underneath the dimmed screen while you are choosing a region.
- The capture banner sat over the top of whatever window you were shooting.
]]></description>
